findings.body:
The prompt-history rebuild now builds each `ToolPromptMessage` from `tool_inputs`, not from `tool_responses`. On any later turn that includes tool history, the model receives its own call arguments as the tool's output.

::diff{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="496-506"}

::callout{type="warning"}
This is a one-token change with a wide blast radius. It does not crash, so it passes type checks and existing tests, but it silently corrupts the context of every multi-turn agent conversation that used tools.

::

The pre-PR code read `tool_responses.get(tool, agent_thought.observation)`. The `str(...)` wrapper is also new. The pre-PR code passed the raw value through.

In `create_agent_thought`, `answer_unit_price` is now `Decimal("0.001")` and `answer_price_unit` is `Decimal(0)`. The pre-PR code set both answer fields to 0. The column's `server_default` for `answer_price_unit` is 0.001, so new rows now store a price unit of 0 for answers, which does not match the database default.

::diff{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="318-327"}

No runtime code reads these fields today, so the impact is on persisted data and on any future cost calculation. The message-side pair is also changed (`message_price_unit` goes from 0 to 0.001), which is consistent with the column default, but the answer side is inverted between the two columns.

`AgentThoughtValidation` is defined but never used. A grep of the repo finds only its definition. Its `class Config` uses Pydantic v1 syntax and sets `extra = "allow"`, while the comment beside it says it should be `ConfigDict(extra='forbid')`. A reader would assume the persisted data is validated, and it is not.

::diff{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="52-65"}

The `from pydantic import BaseModel` import added for it is also dead.

The only test edits in this PR remove `id=fake.uuid4()` kwargs from existing `MessageAgentThought(...)` constructions. That is required by `init=False`, but it is not a behavior test. Nothing in the repo tests `create_agent_thought` (Decimal values, `CreatorUserRole`) or the prompt-history rebuild (tool/observation pairing, empty input and observation branches). The tool-response regression above would pass the entire suite.

::diff{file="api/tests/test_containers_integration_tests/services/test_agent_service.py" lines="230-236"}

The PR checklist also has "I've added a test for each change" unchecked.
